claim.\n\n## 2. Scope and runnable membership\n\nExact selectors: `docs/{qa\u002dlogs,qa\u002dframes,audits,work\u002dlogs,retros,retrospective,futros}/**`,\n`research/**`, `.github/sessions/**`, and singleton\n`docs/reviews/inventory.json`. Survey membership stays unchanged:126149\nrows/22984582 stored lines at inventory source\n`eb4763e3cc9bcd729830cd85f1719bbd4f28db10`, hosted at P1\n`2174265e9cc1b248c0fbe27fa101875984d46d6b`. The generated15392661 CODE\nline tally is not a reading budget. The inventory self\u002drow's134637 lines\nare historical; do not recursively recount the generated output.\n\nThe current cutoff contains127469 selected paths, all blobs:98024 mode100644,\n29445 mode100755, no symlinks/gitlinks. Logical bytes2190843187;\n38355 unique blobs/1084128032 unique\u002dblob logical bytes. These are object\ncontent measures, not packed storage, RAM, disk use or recoverable savings.\nThe prior frozen92e8d07b6163ec5ddd3e9b67f1c42a472b2911d1\u2192cutoff delta is\n799 additions,0 deletions,4 changes,126666 unchanged. Reuse its retained\nmetadata proof; do not rerun earlier accepted survey/audit producers.\n\nKeep three denominators explicit: the historical survey; the cutoff's\ncurrent folder population; the finite reader\u002droute set. Do not change\n`areas.json`, `slices.json`, inventory or historical line counts. The\nold P1\u219292e8 report preserves two deleted credential\u002dlabelled paths as\ncounts/digests only. Never recover/export their names or bodies.\n\nRun this entire block in one shell invocation in the proof clone or actual\nassigned worktree. It reads immutable metadata and writes only compact\npublic\u002droot counts and digests. The directory must not already exist.\n\n```bash\nset \u002deu\nexport LC_ALL=C\nT46_PARENT=$(mktemp \u002dd /tmp/m6\u002dt46\u002dinputs.XXXXXX)\ntaskset \u002dc 8\u002d23 python3 \u002dB docs/qa\u002dlogs/2026\u002d11\u002d03\u002dm6\u002drecords\u002dpreparation/inputs.py \\\n  \u002d\u002drepo \"$PWD\" \u0