tus and navigation sections; do\nnot semantically re\u002daudit every historical transcript or code fence.\nFor the86 anchorless day\u002dlog links, `day\u002drange.py` in the preparation\nfolder is the normative selector. It parses ATX headings at levels2\u20136\noutside backtick/tilde fences (up to three leading spaces). A supported\nheading begins with optional `[label] ` and optional `YYYY\u002dMM\u002dDD `,\n`YYYY_MM_DD ` or ISO date plus `T`, followed by24\u002dhour HH:MM[:SS] and\noptional UTC/Z/+00:00. See its literal TIMESTAMP expression; this is\nsyntax selection, not calendar validity or a claim of UTC for unlabelled\nhistorical times. Indented/setext/HTML headings are unsupported, not\nsilently treated as a match.\n\n\u201cLast\u201d means the last supported timestamp heading in **file order**, not\nthe greatest clock value. Start includes that heading. Stop excludes the\nnext same\u002dor\u002dhigher\u002dlevel ATX heading outside fences, or is EOF. Read at\nmost120 logical lines from that start; `truncated=true` means the rest\nwas not read. A no\u002dmatch result permits only the first40 logical lines\nfor title/date/status, with `last_entry_claim=false`; retain the unknown\nformat rather than guessing or expanding to a full\u002dfile read. Unclosed\nfences are explicit. Parse all heading metadata for index alignment,\nbut never credit earlier entry bodies as read. `\u002d\u002dstdin` returns only\nrange metadata and does not print or execute source text. Its seven tiny\nsynthetic cases are a new selection proof, not a historical\u002dlog audit.\n\nFor inventory.json, inspect generation/source/schema metadata in memory,\nnot its126149 row bodies as prose. The next pointer is historical at this\ncutoff, not this lane's live scheduling authority. Inspect the retros\ndirectory's identity and its already named README, without expansion.\nAmbiguous/dynamic/example references stay classified, not silently skipped\nor resolved by guessing. Directory targets get metadata/index inspection,\nnot recursive body traversal. Binary targets get identities, not readings.\nNo following links into an unbounded second\u002dhop graph.\n\nRecord each reader observation with the referring file/line, literal\nspelling, resolved target/anchor, input identity, exact read range,\nhistorical/current interpretation, concrete reader consequence or N/A,\nand existing next owner. Additional cited text necessary to refute a lead\nis bounded, named and justified before reading; a new broad corpus needs\nroot's scope disposition. Never execute a command copied from a record.\nSuppress sensitive lines before display/export; record a masked range as\nmasked, not a full unredacted reading. No credential\u002dlabelled target is opened.\n\n## 3. Read first and inherited ownership\n\nRead the full #693 thread, records epic, dispatch, plan \u00a7\u00a74\u20138 and order T46.\nRead current seed rules: worktrees, engineering\u002dpractices, issue\u002dtracking,\nmilestone\u002dphase\u002dnaming, adversarial\u002dcouncil, ceremonies, decision\u002dregister,\ninstruction\u002dfiles, learning\u002dcapture, vm\u002dfirst and handheld\u002devidence.\nRead code\u002dauditor's evidence floor and Local methodology, and blindspots\n13/47/51/75. The coordinator's M6 rules are newer than local `next`;\ndo not merge another lane or stale `next` to refresh them.\n\nD\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d184/188/189/209/225 govern table depth, order, ownership,\nno speculative removal and reuse of accepted evidence. D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d223/224\nand #1407 already settle historical journal retention, monthly indexing\nand individual review of33 references/2770 lines (32 edit\u002dscope documents\nplus one unchanged table\u002donly plan). Link counts do not prove non\u002duse.\nThis slice does not implement that backlog or relocate evidence.\n\nPreparation is retained under\n`docs/qa\u002dlogs/2026\u002d11\u002d03\u002dm6\u002drecords\u002dpreparation/`; older metadata context\nis `docs/qa\u002dlogs/2026\u002d11\u002d02\u002dm6\u002dresume/t46\u002dpreparation/`. Make first\nindependent reader observations before opening historical verdicts.\nThen compare the exact accepted T39 bridge: source\n4eb5dfab8e745914a55e7de3e5a43c5b91ebc608, completion\n7994f760fe1f4df6744844e80433bc49295cb94e. All48 named corrected files at\nthe cutoff match pre\u002dcorrection identities; none is missing or unexplained.\nThe accepted correction remains accepted, with integration owned by\n#686/#807/#346. Do not file its absence as a new T46 bug.\n\nOther accepted completion contexts remain separate, not merged members:\nT41 83304388db49e24231158380910067c47ead3f12;\nT42 0eeaa4c9a6d384f57e0017c0be75673eb872f2db;\nT43 fd1238800b61431a8febeebe8cf44f41d2384bbb;\nT44 ad0df587128577212337aa76d171b0b9cfaae4a4.\nUse the coordinator's retained acceptance/completion reports for temporal\ninterpretation, and exact named immutable artifacts only when needed to\nresolve a reader claim. Preserve known missing\u002dinput and custody limits.\nNo accepted application, test, generator, cleanup or old audit is replayed.\n\n## 4. Questions and required tables\n\n| Question | T46 application |\n| \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d |\n| Q1 modernization | Is a current entrypoint sending a reader to a superseded interface or absent current index? Name the current owner and replacement evidence. |\n| Q2 standards | Dates, provenance, scope, actual identity, citation and generated\u002dindex conventions; historical evidence is not rewritten to meet today's format. |\n| Q3 defects | A specific misleading current instruction or broken promised route, with literal trace and self\u002drefutation; distinguish templates, historical commands and pending accepted integration. |\n| Q4 currency | Documentary currency against named source/decision/accepted records; no package release survey or new upstream\u002dversion claim. |\n| Q5 efficiency | Runtime efficiency N/A for a records table; both time\u002dto\u002dplay quantities unmeasured. Report logical metadata cost only, with no savings or cleanup claim. |\n| Q6 reachability | Finite direct reader routes and unproved/ambiguous references; absence from ten entrypoints is not proof of non\u002duse. No removal proposed. |\n| Q7 clarity | Can a new reader identify purpose, date, owner, status, current entrypoint and next action without mistaking history for live authority? |\n\n02 contains: (a) ten disjoint exhaustive root rows with counts/modes/logical\nbytes/unique blobs/digests; (b) historical/current delta reconciliation;\n(c) every retained direct route with its classification and observation;\n(d) one reading row per distinct inspected target/range, including explicit\nunread/binary/directory/unknown cases; (e) inherited accepted\u002downer routes.\nFolder tables may refine public roots into dated groups, but totals must\nreconcile and sensitive path names/bodies must never be exported. No\nblank evidence cell, invented full\u002dread credit or duplicated route key.\n\n## 5. Evidence floor and new controls\n\nCan this be done on the VM? This is immutable documentary/metadata analysis\nand new host record\u002dtool validation. No device\u002druntime behavior is claimed.\nA later source/removal behavior proof requires a separate owning brief and\nGENERIC_X64; none is authorized here.\n\nAllowed: immutable Git metadata, finite named text reads, new audit\u002dlocal\ntable/link/confinement guards, tiny synthetic metadata/Markdown/Git fixtures,\nrecord lints and owning tracker reads/writes. No full tree checkout/export\nfor proof, image/source/archive/cache inspection, fetch, package/config\nevaluation, record\u002dembedded script execution, model provider, guest/build,\ndevice/cloud action, process/host\u002dledger write or other\u002dagent approval.\n\nThe new audit\u002dlocal reader/generator must reject these seven independent\nmutations: omitted folder key; changed source metadata identity; duplicate\nor omitted route key; falsely credited whole\u002dfile reading; intentional\nhistorical/template route relabelled a current defect without evidence;\npending accepted T39 correction relabelled unreviewed/new; and a logical\u002d\nbyte total relabelled disk savings. Retain one complete positive. These\nare future table\u002dvalidation duties, not claims supplied by the input helper.\nThe link parser also proves a valid path/anchor and rejects a missing\ntarget and missing anchor using tiny new fixtures. State its supported\nMarkdown anchor syntax; unsupported syntax remains unknown.\n\nConfinement guard: every commit since seed, not merely final diff, permits\nonly the exact audit root, exact lane pointer, actual\u002ddate worklog and\ngenerated INDEX (later authorized retro). Planted source edit and edit\u002d\nthen\u002drevert histories must fail. Preserve seed/source and frozen accepted\nbytes. Do not let a broad `docs/**` allowlist authorize unrelated records.\n\nFor every new command retain actual argv/cwd/time/exit and both stream\nhashes; inputs/program/fixture versions are separate identities. Preserve\nfailures rather than reconstructing missing receipts. Use existing proof\nclasses tree/history/tool\u002drun/fixture/design and matching PROOF lines.\nCounts certify their actual scope, never historical runtime behavior.\n\nTool interfaces were inspected in preparation/tool\u002dhelp.json and source\nusage. `\u002d\u002dhelp` is unsupported by some helpers: their recorded refusals\nand accidental current\u002drecord checks are not positive help proofs.\nUse `tools/lint\u002daudit\u002dartifacts \u002d\u002dphase pre\u002dissue FOLDER`, then resolution\nwithout that flag after disposition; `\u002d\u002dissue N` checks the audit issue.\n`tools/box\u002dcheck \u002d\u002dissue N`; `tools/work\u002dlog\u002dindex \u002d\u002dwrite/\u002d\u002dcheck`;\n`tools/ceremony\u002dcheck \u002d\u002dgate`; `tools/forbidden\u002dterms\u002dcheck REPO` or\n`\u002d\u002dstdin`. Normal rules/register/hooks/diff checks apply. Sandbox network\nfailure is not an audit PASS; retain it and use the authorized connector\nor approved network execution for a distinct retry.\n\n## 6. Outputs and continuous execution\n\nFixed audit root: `docs/audits/2026_11_03\u002depic\u002dm6\u002drecords/`.\nUse this exact Local JSON shape (also `local\u002dplan\u002dexample.json` in the\npreparation folder), updating identity_source/session from your actual\nobservation. The model namespace is lint normalization, not a provider call.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"depth\": \"local\",\n  \"primary\": {\n    \"harness\": \"Codex\",\n    \"model\": \"openai/gpt\u002d6\u002dastra\",\n    \"lab\": \"openai\",\n    \"effort\": \"xhigh\",\n    \"identity_source\": \"Own observed Codex Herdr footer GPT\u002d6\u002dAstra xhigh; namespace normalized for lint, not provider\u002dattested\"\n  },\n  \"reviewers\": [],\n  \"tier_exception\": \"D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d184\",\n  \"reason\": \"T46 records is a Local table under plan section6c; no external reviewer.\"\n}\n```\n\nA:00\u002drunning\u002dlog.md,01\u002dresearch\u002dnotes.md,stage\u002da/ source/seed binding,\nactual identity and first independent observations. Prove the existing\nlint accepts a tiny Local reviewers[] fixture and refuses a reviewer\u002dcount\nmutation; do not rerun an old audit's positive or negative.\nB:02\u002dforward\u002daudit.md,03\u002dretrospective.md,04\u002danalysis.md,stage\u002db/ with\ntables, reading ranges, ownership, conformance and self\u002drefutations.\nC:05\u002dpunch\u002dlist.md with YAML index; audit\u002dlocal tools/new controls under\ntools/ and stage\u002dc/; second\u002dopinions/review\u002dplan.json with actual primary,\nlab/identity source, Local reviewers[] and D\u002dWORKFLOW\u002d184 reason.\nD: actual pre\u002dissue lint, audit child of693 in M6 with genuine severity/\ncount and observable criteria; 06\u002daudit\u002dsummary.md,\n07\u002dquestions\u002dfor\u